  "question": {
    "text": "<p>A screen is at a distance <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>D</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>80</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math> from a diaphragm having two narrow slits <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> which are <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>mm</mi></math> apart. The slit <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math> is covered by a transparent sheet of thickness <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>2.5&nbsp;</mn><mi>μm</mi></math> and the slit&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> by another sheet of thickness <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1.25&nbsp;</mn><mi>μm</mi></math>&nbsp;​as shown in the figure. Both sheets are made of the same material having a refractive index <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1.40</mn></math>. Water is filled in space between the diaphragm and the screen. A monochromatic light beam of wavelength <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>λ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5000</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mtext>Å</mtext></math> is incident normally on the diaphragm. Assuming the intensity of the beam to be uniform and slits of equal width, calculate the ratio of intensity at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>C</mi></math> to the maximum intensity of interference pattern obtained on the screen, where&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>C</mi></math> is the foot of the perpendicular bisector of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>. [Refractive index of water,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">w</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac bevelled=\"true\"><mn>4</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></math>]</p>\r\r<p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/WhatsApp_Image_2020-05-21_at_8.26.40_PM.jpeg\" style=\"width: 300px; height: 194px;\" /></p>\r",
